        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: protect SMS webhook callback quota [AI]",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where invalid SMS webhook posts could consume the same inbound callback quota used by signed Twilio callbacks when deployments receive traffic through a shared proxy address.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe SMS webhook now parses and validates Twilio-signed form requests, confirms the configured account, and only then applies the fixed-window quota. The quota key is scoped to the SMS account and webhook route plus the client address so one account path cannot consume another account path's quota.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators using the SMS plugin keep the same Twilio signature validation and webhook responses, while invalid unsigned traffic no longer burns the quota for later valid callbacks. High-volume valid signed callbacks are still rate-limited per account route.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAI-assisted change.\n\n- `node scripts/crabbox-wrapper.mjs run --provider aws --idle-timeout 90m --ttl 240m --timing-json --shell -- \"corepack pnpm test extensions/sms/src/webhook.test.ts\"`\n- AWS Crabbox `run_c56fe73f9596`, lease `cbx_979b5ad08666`, `c7a.8xlarge`: `extensions/sms/src/webhook.test.ts` passed 4 tests.\n",
        "branch": "fix/fix-854",
